            "text" : "To calculate **17 × 23**, there are a couple of efficient ways to think about it.\n\n### Method 1: The \"Difference of Squares\" Pattern\nThis is the fastest mental math method. Notice that both numbers are the same distance away from 20 (17 is 3 less than 20, and 23 is 3 more than 20).\n\nWe can rewrite the problem as:\n**(20 - 3) × (20 + 3)**\n\nAccording to the algebraic formula $(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2$:\n1. Square the 20: **20² = 400**\n2. Square the 3: **3² = 9**\n3. Subtract the second result from the first: **400 - 9 = 391**\n\n***\n\n### Method 2: Distributive Property\nIf you prefer breaking the numbers down, you can multiply 17 by 20 and then 17 by 3:\n\n1. **17 × 20 = 340**\n2. **17 × 3 = 51**\n3. Add them together: **340 + 51 = 391**\n\nBoth methods confirm the answer is **391**.",
